--- commit message head
KS-745: the audit export fetches the security service's list route /api/audit and reads data.data.logs

routes/audit-export.ts fetched GET ${SECURITY_SERVICE_URL}/api/audit/logs.
The security service publishes no /logs route, so the path matched
GET /api/audit/:id with id "logs" and answered 404, and the export surfaced
that as a 404 carrying BAD_GATEWAY. It now fetches the list route
/api/audit and reads the list's array, data.data.logs. The old read,
data.data, would have exported the list's wrapper object.

New ks745-audit-export-calls-the-list-route.test.ts: an admin req.user
before the router, fetch stubbed with the list shape. The cell reads the
URL it was asked for and the exported body; the control checks a thrown
fetch still answers 502 BAD_GATEWAY.

Seat edits beyond the READY lines:
- the cell parses the exported body (entries array, totalEntries 1), because
  the READY's substring check passed with the old :144 read;
- a readable URL assertion;
- the file type-checks: the router imported in beforeAll (not a top-level
  await), express's listen type for the server, and a stray second argument
  to the Promise constructor removed.

End-to-end reachability stays UNMEASURED (the ticket's own words): no stack,
and the gateway path /api/admin/audit/export was read, not driven.

Product hunk and cells authored by the local model (Ornith) from a
Wednesday-written brief; source-read by Wednesday; applied and re-run by the
seat A successor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

